  "_commit": {
    "id": "44c8f92c7622afebfe324f9e9792e011caa310e8",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Fix named-key row order, st_join, and several silent wrong results\n\nLayers with a named key are read in the order of their stored keys,\nwhich is neither the file order nor the order the database sorts the\nkeys in (for character keys it is not even sorted). The layer engines\nreturned results in scan order, so layerSubsetByBbox() on a file with\nid = c(3, 1, 2) and x = c(30, 1, 5) returned the rows with x 5 and 30\ninstead of 1 and 5. layerSpatialOverlaps(), layerSubsetByBbox(),\nlayerSubsetByGeometry() and layerSpatialMatch() now map each result\nback to the stored-key order, for a keyed layer and for a keyed table\nin layerSpatialMatch(). Layers numbered by row are unchanged.\nlayerSpatialMatch() also treated every predicate except st_within as\nst_intersects; it now uses the predicate mapping of st_join() and stops\nfor one it cannot express.\n\nst_join() on a DuckDBTable now follows sf::st_join(): a left join by\ndefault (left = FALSE for the old inner join), suffixes on shared\nattribute names, the geometry column last, and a named key kept as a\ncolumn. It no longer returns the internal row_number columns or two\ngeometry columns. This changes the default, so three tests that compared\nagainst inner pair counts now pass left = FALSE.\n\nGeometries given as sf or sfg objects were sent to DuckDB as text with\n7 significant digits, which moved UTM-scale coordinates by metres: for a\npoint at (123456.123456789, 4567890.987654321), st_distance() to the\nidentical point returned 0.0265 and st_intersects() returned FALSE.\nThey are now sent with 17 digits.\n\nSmaller fixes:\n- st_join(), st_join_table(), st_intersects_table() and st_filter()\n  find the geometry column by type instead of assuming \"geometry\".\n- st_union_agg(), st_collect_agg() and st_envelope_agg() accept a table.\n- A geometry column that arrives as wk_wkb (from a duckspatial\n  connection) converts to an sfc.\n- writeGeoParquet() of a lazy table keeps its CRS.\n- geometry_always_xy is set once on the shared connection, so\n  ST_Tr",
    "time": 1794957920
  },
